The 1926–27 Scottish football season was [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]]'s 39th season of competitive football, in which they competed in the [[Scottish First Division]]<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.londonhearts.com/scores/a1920/celtic1927.htm|title=Results for Celtic for 1926-27|website=www.londonhearts.com}}</ref> and the [[Scottish Cup]].

Celtic were unable to retain their league champions title as they ended the season third below [[Motherwell F.C.|Motherwell]] and champions [[Rangers F.C.|Rangers]].

However, their cup campaign proved way more successful as they reached the final for the third year in a row and they managed to win it 3-1 against surprise finalists, Division Two team [[East Fife F.C.|East Fife]].

This was Celtic's 12th Scottish Cup and their 29th major honour, a record at the time.

